Changes of the NTeX distribution
================================

1.2 (940915)

* some minor changes not documented here.
* xdvik, dvipsk, dviljk with kpathsea 2.1 installed
* installed the sauter fonts 2.2
* gsftopk installed

Postscript fonts again (according to the report of Thomas Esser,
te@informatik.uni-ahnnover.de):
* new psfonts.map
* installed new postscript .fd, .adm, .tfm, .vf, .sty files based on a package
  from Sebastian Rahtz in ./fonts/psfonts
* removed the old ps font directories

1.1.4 (940908)

* minor errors in babel installation removed (language.dat now in 
 /usr/lib/texmf/tex/latex/cfg, ...)
* Changed MakeTeXMF for the new font structure ofo DC, FC and CM.
* Change the default font definitions for T1 and OT1. The definitions
  sautercm.fd and sauterdc.fd were removed and replaced by two new
  definitions ntexT1.fd and ntexOT1.fd. Now the DC fonts and the sauter
  CM fonts are appropriately used. (inspired by Thomas Esser and 
  Christian Saucier (saucc00@DMI.USherb.CA))
* eufm works now at size 10 and greater (problem reported by Thomas Esser).
* added an experimental T1fcr.fd to the FC fonts. FC directories changed.
* added some magsteps for pnb10, pnr10, cmr10, cmr25, cmsltt10 in allfonts.lst

Recreating the ps font structure according to the report of
Thomas Esser (te@informatik.uni-hannover.de):
* the psfonts courier, urw, utopia, charter found a place in psfonts and got
  a new structure. ntf-ps package totally recreated.
* installed psfont msym10

* installed psfig

1.1.3 (940907)

* splitted installntex and the configuration scripts. (now in 
  /usr/lib/texmf/tools)
* new directory structure for fc
* added the createallfonts scripts in /usr/lib/texmf/fonts/create to
  repleace the create.sh system. The create.sh are still there (but will
  not be maintained properly).
* xdvi scanning of parameters for specials changed (based on tv001).

1.1.2 (940906)

* cmcyralt is nearly totally replaced by the sauter fonts
* extracm fonts of ams replaced by sauter fonts
* removed/renamed duplicate filenames in /usr/lib/txmf/...
* added ugaritic font
* upgraded arabtex to 3.02b
* the make*font scripts in /usr/lib/texmf/tools now create the pk and the
  tfm directory if it does not exist. Permissions for the scripts changed to
  0744.
* renamed /usr/lib/texmf/tex/plftex/tracefnt.sty to plf_tracefnt.sty
* The fonts hieroglphy, Hebrew, Blackletter, callig15, cherokee, cypriote,
  dingbat, georgian, go, hands, hge, karta, klinz, la, logic, ogham, osmanian
  and thai are now created proberly by create.sh. New metrics created.

1.1.1 (940905)

Changes according to a report of Thomas Esser (te@informatik.uni-hannover.de)
(his detailed report enabled me to improve ntex a lot, THANKS!)
* upgraded LaTeX2e to patchlevel 3
* added isolatin1.sty in /usr/lib/texmf/tex/latex/sty
* apps-default file for xdvi included, configuring with installntex.
* installntex now creates the ls-R database for kpathsea. Could be
  recreated by a shell script in ./tools later.
* directory structure in /usr/lib/texmf changed to speed up kpathsea.
* in installntex lthyphen.cfg will now be linked to lthyphen.babel or 
  lthyphen.latex depending if babel was installed or not.
* changed the permissions for the direcotires/files in /usr/lib/texmf.
  /usr/lib/texmf/fonts/tmp/... is now 1777, all create.sh are now 0700
  the directories are 0755, the files are 0644, the rest of the scripts 
  are 0755.
* installntex now uses /usr/bin/initex to avoid using an old version of initex.
* changed definitions for DocumentPaperSizes in /usr/lib/texmf/ps/config.ps
* install.sh does no longer assume that "." is in PATH.

1.1  (940902)

* removed all pk files from the packages to reduce the size of the 
  distribution.
* thanks to a hint from Benedikt Eric Heinen (beh@icemark.oche.de)  the size 
  of the distribution could be reduced further. I made a terrible mistake...
* added a deskjet driver package. Does not work with the compelte kpathsea 
  directory structure.

1.0

* First release - never made it to a large public
